  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical heater filaments are connected first in parallel and then in series. At the same applied voltage, the ratio of heat produced in same time for parallel to series will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the resistance of the filaments be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and the voltage be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>.</p><p>For the series combination the power is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>For parallel combination,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, the ratio is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}